# External link icons

Sitewide, external links get a ↗ icon via `initExternalLinkIcons()` in `assets/js/scripts-*.js` (runs on load and after dynamic content).

## Do not add icons to

- **Notice board links** — `#noticeContainer`, `#masjid-notice-spotlight`, `#notice-board`
- **Button-style links** — `.btn`, `.contact-action-btn`, `.site-action-btn`, `.btn-campaign`, `.kicc-nav-donate-btn`, `.site-footer-social-link` (icons belong on the button label, not a ↗)
- **WhatsApp links** — `wa.me` / `api.whatsapp.com` URLs, or any link that already shows a WhatsApp icon (`.fa-whatsapp`)
- **Floating action dock** — `.site-action-dock` (WhatsApp, Donate, Back to top)
- Links with `data-skip-external-icon="true"` (set in HTML or JS as `dataset.skipExternalIcon = "true"`)

Notices open poster images in the BaguetteBox lightbox. Buttons and WhatsApp already signal action/channel — a ↗ icon is redundant or misleading.

## When adding new exceptions

1. Set `data-skip-external-icon="true"` on the link in HTML or when creating it in JS, **or**
2. Extend `shouldSkipExternalLinkIcon()` with a stable container selector or helper (`isExternalButtonLink`, `isWhatsAppHref`).

Do not disable `initExternalLinkIcons()` globally for a single section.

## Still show icons on

Inline text links in body copy, nav mega menu off-site links, footer text links, Mixlr archive text links, maps, Kerry Muslim database (non-button), PDF timetable, and other genuine off-site inline navigation.
